  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q04, CamCraft **v0.25.0** (Linux x86_64 release) with SolidCraft **v0.46.2**; minimised by hand.\n\n## What happens\n\nA plate 160 x 70 x 15 mm with a 140 x 50 x 4 mm pocket cut from the top (pocket wall at X = 70) and one Ø6 through hole on that wall (axis at X = 70, Y = 0, so half the hole is 15 mm deep and half 11 mm deep). SolidCraft measures it exactly (volume 139632.434 mm³ = 168000 - 28000 - 9π·13; area 30984.496 mm², also exact; 13 faces, closed).\n\nBoth imports refuse it:\n\n```\nimport_model (.step): corrupt STEP: solid #528 'Body1' could not be tessellated: machining mesh: face 12 capped at 3.307e0 mm sag, tolerance 5e-3 mm - re-export the model, or import an STL\nimport_model (.sc):   Solidcraft design refused: machining mesh: face 12 capped at 3.307e0 mm sag, tolerance 5e-3 mm\n```\n\nFace 12 is the hole's one cylindrical face, whose top edge steps from Z 15 to Z 11 across the wall. 3.307 mm is about the hole's whole span, so the tessellator seems to give up on that face rather than miss by a little. In the full q04 design (R8 and R2 fillets added) the STEP imported but the .sc did not.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe model imports like any closed solid, or the refusal says which face and why in terms a user can act on (\"re-export\" does not help: the file is valid).\n\n## Repro files\n\n- Minimal SolidCraft script [hole-on-pocket-wall.json](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/verify/hole-on-pocket-wall.json) (`solidcraft-cli run hole-on-pocket-wall.json --out x.step`), and its outputs [hole-on-pocket-wall.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/verify/hole-on-pocket-wall.step), [hole-on-pocket-wall.sc](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/verify/hole-on-pocket-wall.sc).\n- MCP: `import_model {\"name\": \"m\", \"path\": \".../hole-on-pocket-wall.step\"}`.\n- Original: [q04-vcarve-sign.sc](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign.sc) (face 19 there).\n\nDone means: hole-on-pocket-wall.step and .sc import (pinned by a solidcore tessellation test on this face shape), with the mesh within the 5e-3 mm tolerance.\n",
